Hate to sound like a know-it-all, but... if you had wished for an amulet of
lifesaving, then this "accident" wouldn't have been fatal. 20/20 hindsight.
Even our local demigod (not me) went through at least one of those amulets.

I remember toasting an amulet of LS when falling down the trapdoor to Hell.
Trouble was, I later fell down that same trap AGAIN without another amulet.
Just call me abysmally stupid. Drowning used to claim my mega-characters 
regularly in version 1.3 (before there were boots of water-walking or amulets
of LS). 

Personally, I'd like to see more ways of avoiding drowning. Seems like when 
you fall in a pool/moat, there should be a few turns, in which time you
could a) pray (surely your god can hear you even when you are underwater), or
b) almost completely disrobe and float to the surface; then, back on shore,
you could figure out a way to get all of your stuff back, whether that consists
of fishing the stuff out piece by piece, freezing/evaporating etc. Note that
your items really take a risk here - scrolls get erased, mucky water could
seep into your potion vessels and spoil them, rust occurs, and if you evaporate
or freeze the water, they take fire/cold risks also.

While I'm on a roll, shouldn't items in a frozen pool or moat be "stuck"?
Currently, I think you can just walk over and pick them up. (I'll check the
code, but I'm pretty sure).

Soliciting discussion on the above...
